  "rawText": "ieweone to Washington, D. €. in the fall of 2940. There,\nI was employed, by the War Department of the United States\n\nGovernment, as a Stock Clerk.\n\nma 943 LT was inducted into the @. S. Navy. 1 served\nas a Boatswain Mate First Class and Acting Company Com-\nmandexr until the end of 1945.\n\nIn 1946, we bought a meat market and restaurant.\n\nIn 1948, I was employed by the Department of Housing\nand Community Development of the U. S. Government. I worked\nmy way up to become Superintendent and Construction Inspector,\n\na position I held until my retirement in 1980.\n\n“I joined the New Bethel Baptist Church in 1951. I sexved\nas Treasurer of the church for about twenty-five years.\n\nIT also served as a Trustee of the church and a member of the\n\nBoy Scouts Committee for thirty years.\n\nMy basic philosophy in life is: Be sure that you are\n\nright; then go ahead.\n\nVERA G. RAGLAND FRANCIS\n\nBorn in Fayetteville, N.C., July 26 1922.\n\nI like to Read, Cook and Exercise.",
  "cleanedText": "ieweone to Washington, D. €. in the fall of 2940. There,\nI was employed, by the War Department of the United States\n\nGovernment, as a Stock Clerk.\n\nma 943 LT was inducted into the @. S. Navy. 1 served\nas a Boatswain Mate First Class and Acting Company Com-\nmandexr until the end of 1945.\n\nIn 1946, we bought a meat market and restaurant.\n\nIn 1948, I was employed by the Department of Housing\nand Community Development of the U. S. Government. I worked\nmy way up to become Superintendent and Construction Inspector,\n\na position I held until my retirement in 1980.\n\n“I joined the New Bethel Baptist Church in 1951. I sexved\nas Treasurer of the church for about twenty-five years.\n\nIT also served as a Trustee of the church and a member of the\n\nBoy Scouts Committee for thirty years.\n\nMy basic philosophy in life is: Be sure that you are\n\nright; then go ahead.\n\nVERA G. RAGLAND FRANCIS\n\nBorn in Fayetteville, N.C., July 26 1922.\n\nI like to Read, Cook and Exercise.",
